  "routeAdjustment": "Before adding a new ramification or uniformizer deformation argument, reuse the exact original full-stabilizer divisibility and E4/E6 multiplicities. Their already proved nonzero analytic germs and native isolated zeros prove nearby ramification is one directly. Native local inverse branches identify the actual descended evaluation functions. A final analytic inverse of the actual uniformizer produces the uniform chart parameter. Native analytic-order derivative comparison replaces a repeated factorization proof. The general external algebraic power-series convergence route remains unnecessary for finite places.",
  "discharged": "Every actual original complex finite place has a locally injective parameter family on one fixed positive-radius disk, with its actual uniformizer equal to the parameter. At every point of that disk and for every nonzero original function, evaluation is meromorphic and has exactly the original normalized place order. Every function regular at that point evaluates analytically there. Native inverse branches of the power map transport the proved original realization away from the center. Existing E4/E6 nonzero germs, native isolated zeros and the full-stabilizer multiplicity theorem show that all sufficiently close noncentral points are unramified. The preceding descended center-order theorem handles the center. The disk radius is independent of the function, and no nearby unramifiedness, analytic representative or order-comparison premise is supplied.",
  "remaining": "Cusp parameters, compatibility of overlapping charts, compactness and the global Abel-Jacobi comparison remain required. Original torsion finiteness/cardinality and comparison back to Qbar divisor classes remain open, followed by Tate realization, rank-two Hecke/Frobenius and inertia comparison, arithmetic automorphy and higher symmetric-power continuation. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
